+10. Close: `bash ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/task-done <ledger> <N> <wt> <tree-after> --probe <package>.patch -- <task test command>`, or `--no-probe "<why>"` in place of `--probe` for a task with no test to probe (docs, config). One command, no shell: a compound `Run:` goes in a `kern-dir tmp` script, passed as `-- bash <path>`. After fix rounds, remake `<package>` from `tree-before`. It writes the complete line only when an approved review saw this tree, the command passes, and the test fails with the change reversed (`probe=ok`) or `--no-probe` gave a reason. A refusal writes nothing and says why. `command exited <n>` or exit 1 (the test passes with the change reversed): return the task to the implementer as the next round (after round 3: the split proposal); `command exited 126` or `127`: stop. Exit 3, an inconclusive probe: rerun with `--no-probe "probe inconclusive: <reason>"` only for a new module or export, or a patch of test files only; else stop and ask. Exit 2: a changed or unapproved tree, review it; a probe error, stop. Under autopilot only, then commit the task's files with `/kern:commit` steps 2 to 6 (a wave task: after step 11).
 11. After a wave, each wave task has been closed in its fork through steps 6 to 10. Apply each worker's patch to the plan worktree one at a time with `bash ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/wt-apply <package>.patch <plan-wt>`, writing `Applied: Task N patch=<path>` after each `applied`. Exit 3 is a conflict with nothing applied: stop. Then `test.full` there; red: stop.
 12. Final review: `ledger-open --summary <ledger dir>` lists the ledger's rulings and minors, then the main checkout's state. Package all with `wt-diff <plan-wt> <base-tree> --out <ledger dir>/reviews/final.diff` (the `Worktree:` line's base tree) and dispatch `kern:task-reviewer` in mode `whole-branch` on `model.final_review` with the package, the plan and that list, to triage which minors block. Re-grade findings by effect. One fix subagent gets the complete findings list (`kern:implementer`, a step 6 brief), each fix red then green; then one `re-review` on `model.final_review` of its diff from `final.diff`'s second line, packaged with an `--allow-file` per task. Residual findings go to the user in step 13.
 13. Finish: report decisions with the cost if wrong, parked items, deferred minors and their triage, verification commands with output, worktree and branch. `ledger-open --summary` must end with `main: unchanged`; anything else goes first in the report. No push or PR, no commit beyond step 10's; offer `/kern:commit` and `/kern:finish-branch`.
